plugin-hostd-protocol (0.21.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: the devel run builds what its build requirements are served for
    (#188)
  * The contract directory has no schema-major level: the readers and the
    domains follow
  * domains: every domain is at 0.1.0, its vocabulary own version, never the
    package one
  * 0.M.m until 1.0: every domain at the package version, 0.21.0
  * same_pass_test: rpm and deb wait for samepass in a needs list too
  * Makefile: the .PHONY continuation the #181 merge broke
  * hosting-verb carries its own translations: the HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS words
    moved from omx-clap-core (ruling R5)
  * release: a merge to devel publishes the real package to staging
  * curve_bind: a unit is matched against omx-dsp's OMX_CURVE_UNIT_WORDS, the
    PARAM_UNITS ids (#184)
  * omx-contract-devel: the name only, no floor (#182)
  * install-contract: every --domain call names the package that installs it
    (#182)
  * public-sources: the served floor runs on every pull request, not only in
    ci.yml's dispatched run (#180)
  * commit-msg hook: the shared stub byte for byte again (no-local-copies was
    red: the stub dropped the FREEMIXER_ names)
  * plugin-hostd-protocol 0.21.0: above the 0.20.6
    python3-plugin-hostd-protocol had under plugin-hostd (#180)
  * libplugin-hostd-protocol0 provides plugin-hostd-protocol, the library's
    RPM name, so plugin-hostd-full installs on Debian (#180)
  * served-floor: a release is refused below the highest version the channel
    ever served any of its packages at (#180)
  * clients/python: leaves_no_mark's docstring is fixed, not carried by a noqa
  * clients/python: the leaves_no_mark docstring carries the noqa the others
    carry
  * C2 findings on #175: the pyc files go, leaves_no_mark() has its Python
    test
  * pin-refused leaves no mark on the plugin: the table half of #121, carried
    from 4aa1524
  * ts: one TypeScript encoder, the client over the codec's Protocol
  * plugin-db's package is no longer rendered here: the build reads nothing
    of plugin-db
  * ci: the shapes job reads omx-contract from this run's branch, not a
    pinned commit
  * abi: the baseline is written again for host_backend_t's param_origin
  * HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS is held to the three golden hosts here, where it lives
    (V29 moved with the item)
  * ci.yml: a pull request into devel may take its packages from the staging
    channel
  * .githooks/commit-msg is the shared stub, byte for byte
  * test-no-clap-core-read: a domain's x-requires that is no list of names is
    refused before anything indexes it
  * No version in prose: abi_clobber names its worker, and no_floors refuses
    "<package> X.Y.Z or later"
  * Review fixes: fuzz records, no_floors arms, x-requires readers, unit ids,
    probe format 2.0
  * test-no-clap-core-read: no packaging/deps.txt to read, and
    info.x-requires is a list of names
  * No hand-kept version floors: deps.txt gone, requirements name packages
    only
  * curve: the unit enumerators by their PARAM_UNITS title,
    OMX_CURVE_UNITS_DB, _DBFS, _KHZ (omx-contract#206)
  * probe output format 2.0: the cost unit is nsPerSample
  * install-contract: every --domain call names the package that installs it
  * protocol: the setting ask_unknown, auto (the default), 1 or 0 (#157)
  * tests: ask_unknown is declared, a word of auto, 1 and 0, default auto
    (#157)
  * What the protocol shares with omx-clap-core is this package's: the build
    reads nothing of it (#67)
  * The pin keys and pin changes words are this package's domain pin;
    protocol.h reads no plugin-db header
  * contract: the domain plugin-hostd-protocol requires host >= 0.35.0
  * Curve unit words read as omx-dsp's B form: OMX_CURVE_UNIT_WORDS, the
    PARAM_UNITS ids (#162)
  * test-no-clap-core-read: the build reads nothing of omx-clap-core (red
    first, #67)
  * curve_points: the marks are one typed word after the count
  * tests: curve_words_test finds omx_curve.h where the compiler does
  * protocol_parse answers a line whose first word is empty; the fuzz models
    skip a blanks-only line (#152)
  * fuzz: the seed corpus carries curve_points' mark count
  * protocol: the ask words of the descriptions store, in the table, the
    grammar and the header (#128)
  * contract: description_get, and -529/-530 widened to the descriptions
    store (#128)
  * contract: the domain plugin-hostd-protocol requires host >= 0.35.0
  * test-client-installed: the client as its consumers get it, installed,
    with no tree on the path
  * PHD_PRESET_FILE_MAX documented as ruled 2026-11-23 (#70): the protocol's
    64 MiB ceiling
  * Revert "PHD_PRESET_FILE_MAX removed: no reader of the protocol applies it"
  * PHD_PRESET_FILE_MAX removed: no reader of the protocol applies it
  * host_dispatch_register_unsupported's doc block wrapped at 120 columns, as
    the rest of the header
  * Every public declaration of the headers documented:
    tools/doxygen.baseline is empty (Fixes #66)
  * fuzz: the records follow src/protocol.c's moved lines, and make test
    holds every record's line (#149)
  * curve: build on omx-dsp #142's unit names (OMX_CURVE_UNIT_WORDS, _D_B)
  * rulings of 2026-11-23: history_get's none words (#86), the preset file
    ceiling (#70)
  * shapes sabotage: each arm is red for the reason it names
  * reply forms and schemas for remote_page_get, note_input, note_drops,
    note_out_drops
  * history_get: the parsed reply tells "unavailable" from "-"
  * make docs-site and docs.yml: the protocol and C API reference published
    per release under /reference/plugin-hostd-protocol/
    (Open-Mixer/.github#242)
  * protocol.h: drop PHD_PRESET_ALIAS_MAX, a macro nothing reads
  * quoted: a backslash inside a quoted word is written and read as \\
  * param_info: the unit word is a PARAM_UNITS standard id
  * plugin-hostd-protocol 0.9.0: VERSION, the spec, debian/changelog and
    package.json
  * codec (TypeScript): one reading of the domains, as the Python codec's;
    the fold left two
  * V16: the words of the protocol are the domain plugin-hostd-protocol,
    named after the package that owns it
  * V16 is on the sorting pass again: the fold's revert 99658e8 is reverted
  * curve_points: the typed prose stays the points' layout, the rendered
    verbs header follows the doc
  * tests: the grammar's curve-origin and curve-leg are omx-dsp's words, with
    a sabotage
  * host-backend.h: param_origin is documented (the doxygen gate)
  * golden: curve_points' replies end with their mark count; the ABNF
    corpus's grammar sum
  * tests: the positional host_backend_t tables carry param_origin's NULL
  * host: curve_points answers the marks a corrector planted
  * protocol: curve_points' reply carries the marks a corrector planted
  * clients/ts: leavesNoMark(code), read from the table
  * clients/ts: a code that leaves no mark, read from the table (red)
  * estimate: the CPU ceiling is the domain's scalar ESTIMATE_CPU_CEILING,
    rendered into protocol.h
  * tests: the CPU ceiling of the insert verdict is the domain's scalar,
    rendered by the generator (red)
  * codec: the TypeScript codec's estimate test reads the verdict and its
    reason
  * estimate: the host's insert verdict is a word of the domain estimate, and
    the reply ends with it
  * tests: the insert verdict of estimate is the host's, its words generated
    from the domain estimate (red)
  * tests: the scratch tree of generated-sabotage.sh copies contract.d
  * pin words: the domain pin is this package's, protocol.h's pin words are
    generated from it (sorting pass, V12)
  * tests: the pin words of protocol.h are generated from the pin domain
    (red; sorting pass, V12)
  * probe words: the domain probe is this package's, protocol.h's lists are
    generated from it
  * tests: the probe words of protocol.h are generated from the probe domain
    (red)
  * commit-msg: the shared stub without the old FREEMIXER names
  * golden: curve_points' replies end with their mark count; the ABNF
    corpus's grammar sum
  * tests: the positional host_backend_t tables carry param_origin's NULL
  * host: curve_points answers the marks a corrector planted
  * protocol: curve_points' reply carries the marks a corrector planted

